{"canonical_record":{"canonical_payload_sha256":"f82faed797bb18b5805333ab90b42cac0943dbe4bbd4ca9aa35b9a8be2c9b270","full_review_record_id":"fullrev_d69be75e7ed21ac1ff9fa8f41113002a0ac58e83a367c4fc06a745cd6a05f125","overall_assessment":"The paper presents a coherent contribution to model-based reinforcement learning by combining Bayesian neural networks with stochastic input variables and alpha-divergence minimization. The primary originality lies in the specific application of this modeling framework to capture complex stochastic dynamics (multimodality and heteroskedasticity) in industrial and benchmark control tasks, as well as the reported solution to the Wet-Chicken problem using a model-based approach.","paper_id":"H1fl8S9ee","paper_identity_sha256":"50d9e5ad29bf06cf5bbb02202d48fc4cb35fe72bb93435e72848d9ccbc6b1fc6","prompt_identity_sha256":"8c882fdfb819041ba1410a35845f5ab0f700cee98e86f0118065600c069c421a","raw_response_sha256":"6a9bd5b920305d6355c26adbaf2c46113f77386b1b295ba93cd27a0f018c8522","request_identity_sha256":"53a25fc59a46832d76129336d2f78bcdd8abc7f41bb6f6cc66341561b616dfaf","reviewer_identity_sha256":"c1cd7c7fdd4a2cbeb45c2f21af982ad0f30bffae8ae148e3eba36479685cf360","role":"ORIG","schema_version":"agentreview-full-review-corpus-v4","structural_context_sha256":"ede3a6569dad33afb5a799fe8188057d517db5713b1a14fbb7ad9528f8ffdb66","subdimension_sections":[{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-005","SRC-028"],"review_text":"The paper does not introduce a fundamentally new problem formulation but rather addresses the existing challenge of model-based reinforcement learning in stochastic dynamical systems. The authors claim to provide the first model-based solution to the Wet-Chicken benchmark, a problem previously solved only via model-free approaches with discretization. While the problem itself is not new, the specific focus on capturing complex stochastic patterns (multimodality and heteroskedasticity) in continuous state spaces using a specific probabilistic model is a meaningful research question within the field.","subdimension_id":"ORIG-PROB"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-004","SRC-007","SRC-016"],"review_text":"The methodology involves extending standard Bayesian neural networks by introducing a random input noise source z to capture unobserved stochastic features. The authors utilize alpha-divergence minimization with alpha = 0.5 for training, citing it as an inference advance that produces better results than variational Bayes. The method is a modification of existing BNN architectures and inference techniques rather than a wholly new algorithmic paradigm, but the specific integration of stochastic inputs with this divergence measure for dynamics modeling is presented as a distinct methodological contribution.","subdimension_id":"ORIG-MTH"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-017","SRC-033","SRC-040"],"review_text":"The paper provides empirical insights into the behavior of different inference methods for BNNs. It reports that alpha = 0.5 is more robust than variational Bayes when the posterior over the noise variable is not fully optimized, and that it captures complex stochastic patterns more effectively. The analysis of the Wet-Chicken problem highlights how the model handles bimodal and heteroskedastic transitions, offering a comparative understanding of why certain methods (like GPs) fail in these specific stochastic regimes.","subdimension_id":"ORIG-ANL"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-005","SRC-034","SRC-038"],"review_text":"The experimental setup includes the application of the proposed method to real-world industrial scenarios, specifically gas turbine control and an industrial benchmark simulator. The use of real-world data with partial observability and the specific configuration of the gas turbine experiment (using a world model to generate artificial batches for robustness testing) adds value beyond standard academic benchmarks. The evaluation on the Wet-Chicken problem in a continuous setting also extends the utility of this existing benchmark.","subdimension_id":"ORIG-EXP"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-004","SRC-017","SRC-022"],"review_text":"The paper combines Bayesian neural networks, stochastic input variables, and alpha-divergence minimization. The rationale for this combination is articulated as a means to achieve both scalability and expressiveness in stochastic patterns, which previous methods achieved only one of. The combination of the BNN with stochastic inputs and the specific alpha-divergence training objective is presented as a synergistic approach that enables the solution of problems where standard variational Bayes or Gaussian processes fail.","subdimension_id":"ORIG-COM"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-017","SRC-033"],"review_text":"The paper includes a critical assessment of variational Bayes (VB) in the context of learning stochastic dynamics. It reports that VB fails completely when the posterior over the noise variable is fixed to the prior, whereas the proposed alpha = 0.5 method still captures complex patterns. This negative result regarding the robustness of VB in this specific setting provides a useful contrast and justifies the choice of the proposed inference method.","subdimension_id":"ORIG-NEG"}]},"disposition":"CANONICAL_FULL_REVIEW_COMMITTED","item_commit_sha256":"663ae76db25508d9532f5f430eb3e6d010d36b13e79c4d04560b3a6e2cdeb57e","paper_id":"H1fl8S9ee","paper_ordinal":91,"raw_attempts":[{"assistant_content_base64":"","assistant_content_sha256":"6a9bd5b920305d6355c26adbaf2c46113f77386b1b295ba93cd27a0f018c8522","attempt_index":0,"error":"","finish_reason":"stop","paper_id":"H1fl8S9ee","raw_provider_response_base64":"","raw_provider_response_sha256":"fde1c095fad070de3b17e76c0f28305422b61f4f41728453649061e49c0ad8a6","request_identity_sha256":"53a25fc59a46832d76129336d2f78bcdd8abc7f41bb6f6cc66341561b616dfaf","role":"ORIG","schema_version":"no-memory-full-review-corpus-build-v5","usage":{"completion_tokens":1065,"prompt_tokens":20946,"prompt_tokens_details":null,"total_